            <ArticleTitle>The passive hamstring stretch test: clinical evaluation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The passive hamstring stretch test is described. Using a modified goniometer it is shown that independent measurements taken by trained examiners approximate very closely to each other. This establishes the test as a valid objective measurement. The possible value of this test as a research tool in low back pain problems is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
